'a']++`, `t` pe `--`. Koi bhi count non-zero to `false`. O(n) time, O(1) space.","en":"If lengths differ, return `false`. Otherwise use a count array of 26: `cnt[c-'a']++` for each char of `s`, `--` for `t`. Any non-zero count means `false`. O(n) time, O(1) space."},"cpp":"class Solution {\npublic:\n    bool isAnagram(string s, string t) {\n        if (s.size() != t.size()) return false;\n        int cnt[26] = {0};\n        for (char c : s) cnt[c - 'a']++;\n        for (char c : t) cnt[c - 'a']--;\n        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++)\n            if (cnt[i] != 0) return false;\n        return true;\n    }\n};"}}